  "proposal": {
    "hypothesis": "At cap 3, a claim survives only after several proclaim-contest-cancel cycles drain three rivals' purses, which is why fee 1 still averages 7 to 8 canceled claims per game. A cap of 2 exhausts rival reserves after roughly one bought contest each, so a claim resolves in fewer cycles while the mandatory fee of 1 stays payable from a typical purse of 1 or 2 and counterplay remains legal and real. The boost (fee plus cost = the whole pocket) becomes a deliberate all-in instead of a routine purchase.",
    "prediction": "Cancellations per game fall by at least 20% on both suites (the frozen bar); claims per game fall; contest_offered_rate stays above 0.60 and can_afford above 0.65; claims crowned without a legal contest stay below 0.10; median rounds fall or stay flat; draws stay within the frozen 0.02 increase.",
    "refutation_evidence": "Cancellations do not fall 20%; or responder affordability drops below the 0.60 floor / offered below 0.50 (poverty closing counterplay, the fee-2 failure mode in miniature); or draws rise past the guard; or the first challenger's win share passes one half; or fewer than three profiles win.",
    "rule_path": "glory.cap",
    "value": 2
  },
